        "Carlton M. Caves",
        "H. Jeff Kimble",
        "Roman Schnabel"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Squeezed light overcame a fundamental measurement-noise limit and became an enabling resource for quantum-enhanced precision measurement, notably gravitational-wave detection.",
        "attribution": "Caves supplied key theoretical foundations, while Kimble and Schnabel represent important experimental development and implementation.",
        "maturity": "The principle is well confirmed, and squeezed-light systems operate in major precision instruments.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The field's experimental milestones and contributors extend well beyond the three names listed."
        ]
